{"id": "EUVD-2026-78780", "enisaUuid": "10d6910b-15dc-36ec-aab9-92451369def8", "description": "A flaw was found in environment-modules. A local attacker can exploit this vulnerability by placing a maliciously named modulefile in a location visible to the victim's `MODULEPATH`. When the victim uses Bash completion for `module` or `ml` commands, the malicious module name, containing shell metacharacters, is evaluated as a command. This can lead to arbitrary command execution in the completing user's shell, impacting their confidentiality, integrity, and availability.", "datePublished": "2026-09-15T15:08:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T02:56:17", "baseScore": 7.3, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:64766", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:80664", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:82919", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:84594", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-85013", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2465635", "https://github.com/envmodules/modules/security/advisories/GHSA-8hrw-p88g-qhmg"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-85013"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2ec73176-da84-3f65-bc17-4b7093bccf8f", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:4.5.2-5.el8_10"}, {"id": "44309f1b-64d5-351b-9a7c-51951290c662", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:5.6.1-2.el10_2.1"}, {"id": "75562cf8-2dad-3229-86d9-f08192bbd00d", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:5.3.0-2.el9_8.1"}, {"id": "c5708c6f-a44b-37a8-8e45-1c0e01e1f6aa", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Hardened Images", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.6.2-1.hum1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c0114